# llama-server API keys -- one per line. '#' starts a comment.
# ANY key listed here is valid, so you can point a client at a different key,
# or give a new device its own, WITHOUT restarting the server.
#
# The file is read at STARTUP ONLY (verified: appending a key returns 401 until
# restart), which is why spares are pre-provisioned rather than minted on demand.
# You only need a restart to REVOKE a key -- see rotate-keys.ps1.
#
# Copy to J:\llama\api-keys.txt and replace these with your own.

# in use -- laptop
correct-horse-battery-staple

# spares -- already valid, just start using one
replace-me-one-two
replace-me-three-four
